> Generated with the AI Coding Tool Validation Kit {{kit_version}}. Complete every `[fill in]` before review. Approval is given by the approver personally in the eQMS (or with an electronic signature); never type a name or signature into this document on someone else's behalf, and never let the AI tool do it.

## 1. Purpose and scope

This document registers {{tool_name}} ({{vendor}}) in the software inventory of {{org_name}}, decides whether its use is QMS-relevant, and defines the intended use for each context of use. It is the input to the requirements ({{doc_id_02}}), the risk assessment ({{doc_id_03}}) and the validation plan ({{doc_id_04}}).

The validation unit is **tool + vendor + surface + context of use**. The language model behind the tool is not qualified as such. What is validated is the intended use, the guardrails around the tool, and the verification of its output. Models are handled through an approved model envelope (section 4) and the model admission check MA-01.

